mod:list_ptr_open_type;
// AN OPEN TYPE HOLDS WHATEVER IS ASKED, AND THE ROOTLESS READER ASKS A POINTER'S POINTEE (DEF-600 with DEF-611, landing 177d2b3). A write through a pointer a call
// returned is a write to what the call's arguments reach, asked by type: a place whose type holds the pointer's pointee is a target (DEF-330, DEF-426). DEF-600: asked
// of a type nobody can read (a generic `T`, `Self`, a `dyn`, a projection), `escape_type_holds` found no member to walk and answered NO. So in a generic body, in a
// trait's default body and over a `dyn` local, `int64->:e = raw fp(raw s.tgt()); discard(raw growh(raw s.tgt()));` wrote to no one and `e` read freed heap, where every
// concrete twin is BORROW-015. It answers YES now, at the type asked and at a member of it (`Bx<T>`, `List<T>`). DEF-611: `escape_pointer_targets`, the reader of a
// pointer that has no place of its own (`growh(raw q.tgt())`), asked a pointer parameter's ref by the pointer's own type alone, where alias.npk's reader of a held copy
// asks its pointee since DEF-426; a concrete `WV->:q` whose `tgt` passes `@self.hv` faulted the same way. It asks the pointee now. The cells stand at FILE level, each
// under its own name as a suffix: an `impl:X:Tr` inside an inline module is TYPE-001 under `npkc` (DEF-463).
// THE LEGEND. `zq_a`, `zq_e`: a local `T:s`, the getter's result used in place and through held copies (DEF-600's four ruled faces are the `gV` and `gW`).
// `zr_f`, `zr_r`: a `T->` parameter, held copies and in place. `zr_i`, `zr_j`: a by-value parameter used in place, and through held copies. `zr_s`, `zr_t`: a trait's
// default body over `Self->`, in place and held copies. `zr_d`, `zr_e`: a `dyn Lk` local. `zr_b`, `zr_l`: only a MEMBER is open, a `T` held by value in `Bx<T>` and a
// `List<T>`. `zr_a`: the getter takes a second pointer (`tga(Self->:self, It->:ip)`) and the take's receiver and the growth's are two parameters, so only that pointer's
// pointee ties them; `r` and `f` a pointer parameter in place and through copies, `i` and `j` a by-value parameter. `zr_x_hL`: DEF-611 over a `List` member itself
// (`lx` passes `@self.l2`). `zt1`, `zt2`: the STORE side through the getter (BORROW-002, on every build).
// THE SUFFIX. `g` generic, `h` its concrete twin; `V` at `WV` (`tgt` passes `@self.hv`), `W` at `W` (`tgt` passes the pointer member `self.hp`), `A` at `WA` (the
// projection `T.It` is `WV`). DEF-611's concrete faces are `zr_r_hV`, `zr_ar_hA` and `zr_x_hL`; the other `h` cells were refused before this row.
// THE PROJECTION CELLS (`zr_a*_gA`) ARE THE CHECKER'S ALONE: a parameter of type `T.It` is refused where its function is instantiated (TYPE-001; DEF-377 and DEF-489,
// open), so no program holding one builds, and their controls `zr_a*_gAc_ok` (the take with no growth) stand HERE, where they must stay silent.
error:E5;
